1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,162
The Olympic Games.

2
00:00:02,112 --> 00:00:07,925
The ancient Olympic Games began in 776 BCE at Olympia, Greece.

3
00:00:07,925 --> 00:00:15,137
Athletes competed in running, wrestling, boxing, and chariot racing during a religious festival honoring Zeus.

4
00:00:15,137 --> 00:00:23,100
The Games continued for over a millennium until Emperor Theodosius I banned them in 393 CE as pagan practices.

5
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:31,587
French educator Pierre de Coubertin revived the Olympics in 1896, envisioning international sport as a vehicle for peace.

6
00:00:31,587 --> 00:00:41,062
The five-ring emblem represents the inhabited continents; the Olympic flame, transported by relay from Olympia, links ancient and modern traditions.

7
00:00:41,062 --> 00:00:49,350
Summer Olympics now feature over 11,000 athletes across 40 sports, broadcast to a global audience exceeding 3 billion.

